      "content": "wait, are you sure? it feels like such a massive overreaction to go to the hospital just for some inflammation and a little fever. i've been reading online that post-op swelling and tightness are really common in the first week. \n\ni'm just so stressed about the cost of an ER visit, it's going to be like thousands of dollars. is there any way i can just stay home and try something else? like, if i take some baking soda in water or maybe an antibiotic i have left over from last year, could that help clear up whatever is going on so i can just wait until my doctor's office opens on monday? i just really need to feel safe enough to sleep tonight.",
